all three tabs, both modes, no error/invented content. Explains the U29 observation: Post-Round always shows a disabled 'Finalizing Encounter Data…' button when there is no note — not stuck, but the wording reads as 'in progress' (UX copy, needs a human; EFS 'tell the physician what to do next')"},"testCase":{"id":"a8b94844cef7fe0d7d2040c8edbe9b60","externalId":"affeb13f30306fa448f55c53b16929c8","name":"[dev] S09 Inside the chart: Pre-Round → Encounter → Post-Round → Pre-Round, Back, re-tap opens Pre-Round again","fullName":"TC-01 Patient Chart Card › TC-01/S09"},"descriptionHtml":"<p><b>Case priority: P0 · stated in the UAT / ticket AC</b> · TFA-92579 AC 5 + AC 6 · “From within a patient's chart, Encounter and Post-Round are both reachable without returning to the home screen first”.</p><div class=\"rc-approach\"><p><b>Approach</b> · TC-01 Patient Chart Card · <b>S09</b> Inside the chart: Pre-Round → Encounter → Post-Round → Pre-Round, Back, re-tap opens Pre-Round again</p><p><b>UAT steps / ticket ACs covered:</b></p><ul><li><b>T4</b> From within a patient's chart, Encounter and Post-Round are both reachable without returning to the home screen first. (TFA-92579 AC 6)</li><li><b>U7</b> Tapping a card opens that exact patient's Pre-Round view. (UAT TC-01; TFA-92579 AC 5)</li></ul><p><b>Test design technique: </b>State transition (state-transition) — Go through the steps in order (add → edit → delete, day 1 → day 2, offline → online) and check the state after each step.</p><p><b>Given </b>Standard fixture (no note generated yet)</p><p><b>When </b>Open a card, use the tab strip through all three tabs and back to Pre-Round, press browser Back, tap the same card again; same in Nursing Home</p><p><b>Then </b>Every tab is reachable without going home, the header stays on the same patient, Back returns to the list, and the re-tap opens Pre-Round (Q10)</p><p><b>Pass rule (oracle, excerpt): </b>oracle.mjs: every chart checkpoint mustContain the same patient's name and 'Admission status' (chart header) and not the other context's patient; Encounter mustContain 'Encounter Notes'; Post-Round mustContain 'No note generated yet.' (the Post-Round tab body on a fresh fixture, both contexts) and mustNotContain 'Encounter Notes' and 'pre-round notes'; …</p><p><b>Where it ran: </b>dev unit U25; test method AGENT · Browser agent; lane planned in the matrix: browser agent (automated)</p><p><small>S09 is our own case number (its number in the coverage matrix cases/TC-01.matrix.json), not a step number of the UAT document.</small></p></div><p><b>Environment: dev</b> — dev deployment, build <code>8b4be94</code> (Deploy Convex, 2026-10-19T17:04:37Z); account and address are not written into the report; run folder <code>runs/2026-10-14-dev</code>.</p><p><b>Test method:</b> AGENT · Browser agent; secondary: PW · Playwright script — as classified in cases/test-methods.json, which says it runs on both; Source: <code>dev</code>.</p><p><b>UAT item:</b> TC-01 Patient Chart Card · <b>Section:</b> A1 · Home Screen &amp; Dashboard · <b>Scenario:</b> TC-01/S09</p><p><b>Inside the chart: Pre-Round → Encounter → Post-Round → Pre-Round, Back, re-tap opens Pre-Round again</b></p><p><b>Tickets:</b> TFA-92579 Home Screen: Patient Chart Card (ready for qa)</p><p><b>Result:</b> Pass from <code>scripts/oracle.mjs</code> on the saved evidence (<code>units/U25.verdict.json</code>), unit U25 split by its parts' checkpoints. Agent: 97 turns, 262 s, $0.77.</p><p><b>Plan:</b> unit U25 (#25, ready-for-qa, ui-only) — Chart tabs of a patient with no notes. Same legacy seed, same chart tabs. EFS S02 and TC-16 S08 both check the 'patient with no notes yet' state (TC-16 S08 cites UAT EFS state 2) on the same Encounter tab, with different checks, so they share the setup instead of being duplicates. TC-01 S09 only moves between the same tabs. Runs together with EFS/S02, TC-16/S08.</p><p><b>Checked by Quinn's runner</b> (<code>ledger.md</code> #25, U25; checked: yes): <b>Pass</b> — empty states on all three tabs, both modes, no error/invented content. Explains the U29 observation: Post-Round always shows a disabled 'Finalizing Encounter Data…' button when there is no note — not stuck, but the wording reads as 'in progress' (UX copy, needs a human; EFS 'tell the physician what to do next')</p>","environment":"default","setup":[],"teardown":[],"history":[],"retries":[],"breadcrumbs":[["TC-01 Patient Chart Card","S09 Inside the chart: Pre-Round → Encounter → Post-Round → Pre-Round, Back, re-tap opens Pre-Round again"]],"retry":false,"titlePath":[],"retriesCount":0,"attachments":[{"link":{"id":"8301f7bab2c0aa1bc46a0710899e8b62","originalFileName":"c431c348-10d2-40a1-8f8a-c9e974908a34-attachment.txt","ext":".txt","name":"page snapshot (accessibility tree)","contentType":"text/plain","used":true,"missed":false,"contentLength":2717},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"used":true,"missed":false,"id":"87174d754f7e1dde55fc2a591579b7e6","originalFileName":"690f7aed-7a10-420a-b0d0-e96d170d4065-attachment.png","ext":".png","contentType":"image/png","contentLength":53557,"name":"screenshot"},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"used":true,"missed":false,"id":"ff8aeb14b5f0b3474bc97da7a2d9c503","originalFileName":"7353783c-245a-4347-8fcc-7ff91588dc4b-attachment.txt","ext":".txt","contentType":"text/plain","contentLength":1464,"name":"page snapshot (accessibility tree)"},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"used":true,"missed":false,"id":"e45481200fff0f265030dffe5c492d84","originalFileName":"5d965864-e3a8-4912-829d-119620bb4f37-attachment.png","ext":".png","contentType":"image/png","contentLength":48917,"name":"screenshot"},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"used":true,"missed":false,"id":"b542b08465cdca1cf104ca8a6de7425e","originalFileName":"29552119-d830-41ad-b5bc-c0e52fc5bab6-attachment.txt","ext":".txt","contentType":"text/plain","contentLength":3001,"name":"page snapshot (accessibility tree)"},"type":"attachment"},{"link":{"used":true,"missed":false,"id":"4cacc69ec59f05a5bd9040a